To scan all service versions running on an IP address, use Nmap (Network Mapper). It is the industry-standard tool for banner grabbing and service version detection. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] 
## The Recommended Command
Run this command in your terminal (requires sudo for accurate OS and service tracking): [6, 7] 

sudo nmap -sV -sC -p- -T4 192.168.1.1

(Replace 192.168.1.1 with your target IP address) [8, 9] 
## Breakdown of the Flags Used

* -sV: Service Version Detection. Probes open ports to determine exactly what software and version is running.
* -sC: Default Scripts. Runs safe, built-in Nmap scripts to gather deeper configuration info and vulnerability data from the services.
* -p-: Scan All Ports. Forces Nmap to scan all 65,535 possible ports instead of just the top 1,000.
* -T4: Timing Template. Speeds up the scan so it finishes faster without being overly aggressive. [10, 11, 12, 13, 14] 

