## Alternative: Fast Scan First (Saves Time)
Scanning all 65,535 ports with version detection can take a long time. A faster strategy is to find open ports first, then scan only those open ports for versions: [15, 16, 17] 

# 1. Quick port discovery (saves open ports to open_ports.txt)
sudo nmap -p- --open -oG open_ports.txt 192.168.1.1
# 2. Targeted version scan on found ports
sudo nmap -sV -sC -p $(awk '/Ports:/{gsub(/[a-zA-Z\/]/,""); print $5}' open_ports.txt | tr '\n' ',') 192.168.1.1

## Alternative: Masscan (For massive networks or speed)
If you need to scan an entire subnet or multiple IPs incredibly quickly, use Masscan to find open ports, then feed them into Nmap. [18, 19, 20, 21, 22] 

sudo masscan -p1-65535 192.168.1.1 --rate 1000

